WEBVTT

00:00:08.800 --> 00:00:09.970
What?

00:00:09.970 --> 00:00:14.980
Makura Research Laboratories
You want to know the antibody reactions
towards a new type of deadly virus?

00:00:14.980 --> 00:00:18.480
Oh, I see. This one's very difficult.

00:00:18.480 --> 00:00:21.380
This one involves risking someone's life.

00:00:22.020 --> 00:00:25.510
What?! You'll add fifty percent to my usual fee?!

00:00:25.750 --> 00:00:31.850
Send me the data. When I find a suitable
person, I'll start the experiments.

00:00:34.060 --> 00:00:36.730
Why didn't you bring it? Huh?!

00:00:36.730 --> 00:00:38.320
What's the meaning of this?

00:00:38.970 --> 00:00:40.430
Are you listening?

00:00:41.770 --> 00:00:44.710
Wasn't our deal that you'd have it by today?

00:00:44.710 --> 00:00:47.040
How much longer are you going
to make us wait?

00:00:47.580 --> 00:00:49.600
Are you jerking us around or something?

00:00:49.780 --> 00:00:51.250
Take that.

00:00:52.310 --> 00:00:53.650
She pisses me off.

00:00:53.650 --> 00:00:56.890
Forget about her. This is so stupid. Let's go!

00:00:56.890 --> 00:00:59.420
Man, what a waste of time.

00:00:59.420 --> 00:01:00.490
Really.

00:01:00.360 --> 00:01:01.460
Yeah.

00:01:25.080 --> 00:01:27.510
What's the point if you don't
get up on your own?

00:01:36.890 --> 00:01:41.990
I really want to be just like you, Mikura, but...

00:01:48.770 --> 00:01:53.710
<i>Preferential Treatment</i>

00:02:05.050 --> 00:02:07.050
<i>Norikonda sabaibaru cousutaa</i>

00:02:05.050 --> 00:02:07.020
The survival roller coaster we got on

00:02:07.020 --> 00:02:09.790
There's no need to give up,
run by the highway

00:02:07.050 --> 00:02:09.490
<i>Akirame muyoude run by the highway</i>

00:02:09.490 --> 00:02:11.360
<i>Kimiwa inochi karagara</i>

00:02:09.790 --> 00:02:11.560
You just barely escaped with your life

00:02:11.360 --> 00:02:13.890
<i>Atashitachimo nodoga karakara</i>

00:02:11.560 --> 00:02:14.160
We're thirsty

00:02:13.890 --> 00:02:16.090
<i>Kyokugento mugendai</i>

00:02:14.160 --> 00:02:16.300
Extremities and infinity

00:02:16.090 --> 00:02:18.430
<i>Tomo ni sorette mugendai</i>

00:02:16.300 --> 00:02:18.660
Together, they form a fantasy

00:02:18.430 --> 00:02:20.330
<i>Kamaeta me hibana chiri</i>

00:02:18.660 --> 00:02:20.530
The eyes, squaring away, are
throwing out sparks

00:02:20.330 --> 00:02:23.360
<i>Oni-san kochira to shita o dasu</i>

00:02:20.530 --> 00:02:23.590
"You're it! This way, " you say,
as you stick your tongue out

00:02:24.500 --> 00:02:25.590
<i>Wink</i>

00:02:24.670 --> 00:02:25.660
Wink

00:02:27.270 --> 00:02:29.270
<i>Kyouretsuna itamini kansha</i>

00:02:27.510 --> 00:02:29.480
Grateful for the excruciating pain

00:02:29.270 --> 00:02:31.610
<i>Power to iu na no rei de henkan</i>

00:02:29.480 --> 00:02:31.910
I'm restored by a gratitude
known as power

00:02:31.610 --> 00:02:37.520
<i>Mou sorosoro okaeri asobareta houga
iinodewa naide shouka</i>

00:02:31.910 --> 00:02:37.720
Perhaps it would be better too return soon?

00:02:37.520 --> 00:02:46.420
<i>Matsugeno sukima umeruyouni aimeiku</i>

00:02:37.720 --> 00:02:46.660
As though filling in the gaps between
the eyelashes, eye make

00:02:46.420 --> 00:02:53.730
<i>Kokorono sukima umeruyouni I take</i>

00:02:46.660 --> 00:02:53.930
As though filling in the gaps of
my heart, I take

00:02:53.730 --> 00:02:58.200
<i>Gekiretsu panchide gyakuni takamaru</i>

00:02:53.930 --> 00:02:58.400
On the contrary, the intensity is heightened
by a powerful punch

00:02:58.200 --> 00:03:02.670
<i>Yabai shiuchi hodo yokei moechauwa</i>

00:02:58.400 --> 00:03:02.740
The worse I'm treated, the more I get fired up

00:03:02.670 --> 00:03:07.040
<i>Mouretsu panchide atashi takaburu</i>

00:03:02.740 --> 00:03:07.180
I get worked up over an intense punch

00:03:07.040 --> 00:03:15.470
<i>Sonna koto shite kurete arigatou</i>

00:03:07.180 --> 00:03:16.020
Thank you for doing such a thing

00:03:16.090 --> 00:03:17.990
<i>Sukima sukima sukimani mimai</i>

00:03:16.260 --> 00:03:18.190
A gap, a gap, pay a sympathy visit

00:03:17.990 --> 00:03:19.990
<i>Janai janai itainjanai?</i>

00:03:18.190 --> 00:03:20.160
Doesn't it, doesn't it, doesn't it hurt?

00:03:19.990 --> 00:03:21.660
<i>Mimai tsurai? ltai? Yabai?</i>

00:03:20.160 --> 00:03:21.930
Is the visit painful? Does it hurt?
Is it dangerous?

00:03:21.660 --> 00:03:26.290
<i>lkitai itai shitai, lkitai itai shitai</i>

00:03:21.930 --> 00:03:26.600
I want to go, I want to stay, I want to do it

00:03:30.610 --> 00:03:34.300
Ms. Mikura's gone off to the local
neighborhood exercise class?

00:03:35.280 --> 00:03:39.300
Yeah, she's gotten into it quite a bit recently.

00:03:40.320 --> 00:03:42.150
A pair of tickets?

00:03:42.150 --> 00:03:44.720
To the virtual reality attraction, which
is all the rage these days.

00:03:44.720 --> 00:03:46.590
Virtual what?

00:03:46.320 --> 00:03:50.830
<i>Shell of Thoughts</i>

00:03:47.060 --> 00:03:52.330
I've wanted to try it once. I applied for a
chance at being a volunteer.

00:03:52.330 --> 00:03:54.820
I won the sweepstakes and get to try
the machine for free.

00:03:55.060 --> 00:03:58.370
Asami, I didn't know you had an
interest in this kind of thing.

00:03:58.370 --> 00:04:00.040
It's that thing, right?

00:04:00.040 --> 00:04:03.200
Like the thing where you can see
any dream you want.

00:04:03.200 --> 00:04:05.370
It's that escapism thing, right?

00:04:05.370 --> 00:04:06.510
This thing...

00:04:06.270 --> 00:04:07.410
Mr. Kurokawa!

00:04:12.680 --> 00:04:15.620
Well, would you like to go with me?

00:04:16.150 --> 00:04:17.990
I'm going home.

00:04:17.990 --> 00:04:19.540
That didn't go very well.

00:04:22.390 --> 00:04:24.630
Well, what's the big deal about
it not going well?

00:04:24.630 --> 00:04:27.330
These things are dependent on the programmer.

00:04:27.330 --> 00:04:31.470
If someone unskilled makes the program,
it'll turn into a nightmare.

00:04:31.470 --> 00:04:34.490
In the worst case scenario, you can
end up frying your brain.

00:04:34.740 --> 00:04:37.500
In other words, there's a lot of danger involved.

00:04:38.040 --> 00:04:40.710
In other words, could I possibly be an old man,

00:04:40.710 --> 00:04:42.210
I mean, the person who saved Asami's life?

00:04:42.210 --> 00:04:44.350
I think it would be the former.

00:04:44.350 --> 00:04:45.950
Oh?

00:04:44.850 --> 00:04:47.050
She probably thinks of you as a disgusting
middle-aged man

00:04:47.050 --> 00:04:50.090
who doesn't understand a naive young
maiden's feelings.

00:04:50.090 --> 00:04:51.780
Oh, why?

00:05:00.830 --> 00:05:02.160
Hey, you!

00:05:02.160 --> 00:05:03.990
Rub, rub, rub, rub!

00:05:15.080 --> 00:05:16.170
Ennui...

00:05:33.160 --> 00:05:36.820
Again! They didn't even bother
to lock the door. Jeez!

00:05:38.970 --> 00:05:40.900
Virtual experience?

00:05:47.080 --> 00:05:48.510
Do you have anyone accompanying you?

00:05:48.510 --> 00:05:50.610
What? It's not all right to be alone?

00:05:50.610 --> 00:05:52.580
In that case, I'll go through the
experiences of two people.

00:05:52.580 --> 00:05:55.480
Oh, no, that's quite all right.

00:05:57.250 --> 00:05:58.550
Is this all right, then?

00:05:58.550 --> 00:06:01.960
Thank you. The more detailed the data,

00:06:01.960 --> 00:06:04.450
the better we can create the dream you desire.

00:06:05.060 --> 00:06:06.960
I see.

00:06:11.230 --> 00:06:16.370
As you know, the outside facilities are
being constructed in Dezney Park.

00:06:16.370 --> 00:06:18.470
While this is just the system alone,

00:06:18.470 --> 00:06:21.310
there's no problem with its functionality.

00:06:33.860 --> 00:06:35.850
All right! Let's begin!

00:06:37.530 --> 00:06:41.890
Brain waves normal. No abnormalities with her
pulse. She's in R.E.M. sleep.

00:06:42.600 --> 00:06:44.160
Synchronizing with the data.

00:06:53.170 --> 00:06:55.470
The subject's data is being output.

00:06:59.450 --> 00:07:01.540
Whoa! This is...

00:07:02.220 --> 00:07:04.420
We have a volunteer.

00:07:04.420 --> 00:07:08.580
Let's gauge any changes within her body
due to some misalignments.

00:07:09.890 --> 00:07:11.960
When we put this thing into real service,
there's a possibility the dream...

00:07:11.960 --> 00:07:14.860
The dream might turn into a nightmare.

00:07:14.860 --> 00:07:17.230
I want some data for when we need
to counteract that.

00:07:17.230 --> 00:07:19.730
But we don't have her consent.

00:07:19.730 --> 00:07:21.760
It's a simulation of an unexpected accident.

00:07:22.040 --> 00:07:24.940
If she knows, then there would be no
point to it, would there?!

00:07:25.970 --> 00:07:27.340
Understood.

00:07:33.280 --> 00:07:35.310
She's the suitable person.

00:07:35.480 --> 00:07:36.880
What?

00:07:39.150 --> 00:07:40.660
A pair of tickets?

00:07:40.660 --> 00:07:42.990
To the virtual reality attraction which
is all the rage these days.

00:07:42.990 --> 00:07:44.580
Virtual what?

00:07:45.030 --> 00:07:48.790
Wow, I didn't know you had such an
intense interest in these things.

00:07:49.060 --> 00:07:52.670
Hey, I don't have time to do this.

00:07:52.670 --> 00:07:54.240
I'm late, late!

00:07:54.240 --> 00:07:56.470
I'm going to get fired from the company.

00:07:56.870 --> 00:07:58.270
I'm on my way!

00:07:58.510 --> 00:08:00.060
Have a nice day.

00:08:01.040 --> 00:08:03.240
Something's strange...

00:08:05.050 --> 00:08:09.280
It's that thing, right? Like the thing where you
can see any dream you want.

00:08:09.750 --> 00:08:12.740
It's that escapism thing, right, this thing?

00:08:13.560 --> 00:08:17.550
Mornings are great with pleasant smelling toast,
though. Whoopee! Yay for bread!

00:08:17.960 --> 00:08:21.260
Pops, who's nuts for noodles, eating toast?!

00:08:22.200 --> 00:08:25.170
Something is definitely strange.

00:08:35.010 --> 00:08:38.110
Why can't I live an elegant life in the castle,

00:08:38.110 --> 00:08:40.480
and experience good things to look
back on like I want to?

00:09:40.110 --> 00:09:41.940
And now, it's you?!

00:09:43.410 --> 00:09:45.080
I hope you're ready for the worst.

00:09:45.080 --> 00:09:46.550
Ready for what?

00:09:46.550 --> 00:09:49.580
I only want to live an elegant life as a princess.

00:09:49.580 --> 00:09:50.920
Don't waste your breath!

00:09:51.650 --> 00:09:53.350
You've come all this way just to...

00:09:53.620 --> 00:09:55.620
Hey, wait a minute!

00:09:55.620 --> 00:09:59.130
Why do you have a sword and I'm unarmed?

00:09:59.130 --> 00:10:00.660
That's not fair!

00:10:00.660 --> 00:10:02.860
I have no use for your nonsense.

00:10:02.860 --> 00:10:04.420
Say your prayers!

00:10:05.300 --> 00:10:07.670
What the hell is this?!

00:10:11.210 --> 00:10:12.940
What? What's the matter?

00:10:12.940 --> 00:10:14.340
Kaima is out of control!

00:10:14.980 --> 00:10:16.640
There are abnormalities within the
autonomic nervous system!

00:10:16.640 --> 00:10:19.680
Our controls are not working!

00:10:19.680 --> 00:10:21.380
Out of the way!

00:10:21.380 --> 00:10:23.580
How's that? Is there a change?

00:10:23.580 --> 00:10:25.090
No change!

00:10:25.090 --> 00:10:28.060
Rise in blood pressure!
Controls not responding!

00:10:28.460 --> 00:10:29.720
This is a disaster!

00:10:29.720 --> 00:10:33.630
Is this the new type of deadly virus doing
something beyond the expected?

00:10:38.270 --> 00:10:42.200
<i>Makura Research Laboratories</i>

00:10:44.570 --> 00:10:45.800
Here?

00:10:46.440 --> 00:10:49.640
Makura Research Laboratories,
this is certainly the place.

00:10:49.840 --> 00:10:50.910
Hey, hey...

00:10:50.580 --> 00:10:51.780
What's the matter?

00:10:51.780 --> 00:10:53.680
The tickets... Forgot 'em.

00:10:55.150 --> 00:10:57.340
Hey, hey, hey, hey.

00:11:05.290 --> 00:11:08.750
Since there was no answer, we just
happened to go in on our own.

00:11:10.370 --> 00:11:12.160
No one's here.

00:11:12.770 --> 00:11:14.830
Not only are they careless, they're
sloppy with security too.

00:11:15.440 --> 00:11:18.600
Huh? What's my ticket doing here?

00:11:18.770 --> 00:11:22.770
Hey, for real. But how did it teleport here?

00:11:25.280 --> 00:11:27.180
Isn't it a little noisy?

00:11:30.720 --> 00:11:32.580
Ms. Mikura!

00:11:34.720 --> 00:11:36.660
Maretrix Box?

00:11:36.960 --> 00:11:37.950
That thing?

00:11:38.730 --> 00:11:43.290
Yes, it's the new trial system.

00:11:44.230 --> 00:11:48.040
There wasn't anything wrong with its
functionality or so we thought, but...

00:11:48.040 --> 00:11:51.370
This was just a trial run with a volunteer
for advance advertisement.

00:11:51.710 --> 00:11:53.170
Was?

00:11:53.170 --> 00:11:56.040
There wasn't anything wrong with its
functionality or so we thought?

00:11:56.040 --> 00:11:58.210
What's that supposed to mean?

00:11:58.210 --> 00:12:00.380
Seriously, what do you mean by that?

00:12:00.380 --> 00:12:03.580
What? You're not from the parent company?

00:12:03.580 --> 00:12:05.550
We're relatives of the girl in there, you idiot.

00:12:05.550 --> 00:12:08.960
While there's not supposed to be
any danger whatsoever,

00:12:08.960 --> 00:12:11.590
She, for whatever reason,

00:12:11.590 --> 00:12:14.220
isn't able to come back

00:12:14.660 --> 00:12:17.830
from her own dream world.

00:12:23.270 --> 00:12:25.310
Why did she get into that thing?

00:12:25.310 --> 00:12:28.140
Mikura's full of curiosity and always
ready to take a stab at things, so...

00:12:49.700 --> 00:12:51.690
What's the point if you don't
get up on your own?

00:13:02.710 --> 00:13:04.800
What can be done to save her?

00:13:31.740 --> 00:13:33.830
What the hell is this place?

00:13:47.820 --> 00:13:49.450
Omabari?

00:13:50.790 --> 00:13:55.460
We are investigating your criminal activities
thoroughly! Behave yourself!

00:13:55.460 --> 00:13:57.400
You put me in this position

00:13:57.400 --> 00:13:59.630
so how the hell am I supposed to
behave better than this?!

00:14:01.170 --> 00:14:04.800
In that case, it's time for a close investigation!

00:14:13.080 --> 00:14:15.780
Asami, are you really going to do this?

00:14:17.120 --> 00:14:18.150
Mikura!

00:14:18.150 --> 00:14:21.550
No! You touch her now and you'll
do irreparable damage!

00:14:22.390 --> 00:14:25.150
Why is the setting only for girls?

00:14:25.330 --> 00:14:27.160
If we switch now,

00:14:27.160 --> 00:14:28.920
the current subject will be exposed
to additional danger.

00:14:29.100 --> 00:14:33.030
But isn't jumping into Mikura's dreams,

00:14:33.030 --> 00:14:34.800
then dragging her out from there
too violent a method?

00:14:34.800 --> 00:14:36.170
In case of emergencies,

00:14:36.170 --> 00:14:40.200
we did prepare a rescuer program for
customers to wake them up.

00:14:40.470 --> 00:14:43.480
However, we had a little bit of trouble

00:14:43.480 --> 00:14:46.570
and it stopped responding to our controls.

00:14:46.810 --> 00:14:49.720
This is really going to be all right, correct?

00:14:49.720 --> 00:14:52.720
She won't end up pointy-haired
like Harada, will she?

00:14:52.720 --> 00:14:56.460
Well, yes. It also depends on her
psychological strength though.

00:14:56.460 --> 00:14:59.760
Depends? Depends, my ass!
Why you! Why you!

00:14:59.760 --> 00:15:01.460
Please, hurry.

00:15:09.740 --> 00:15:12.300
Well, we'll start synchronization. Hey!

00:15:17.280 --> 00:15:19.800
I'm going to save Ms. Mikura!

00:15:26.450 --> 00:15:29.620
Hey! That's disgusting!

00:15:29.620 --> 00:15:31.530
Cut that out!

00:15:31.530 --> 00:15:32.650
Cut it out!

00:15:34.330 --> 00:15:36.060
That's disgusting!!

00:15:35.230 --> 00:15:37.060
Playtime is over.

00:15:36.060 --> 00:15:39.790
Let me go! Wait...

00:15:37.060 --> 00:15:39.790
Now, I'll have you fall unconscious in agony.

00:15:58.950 --> 00:16:02.510
Asami? What's she doing here?
Is this Asami's...

00:16:04.230 --> 00:16:07.630
Ms. Mikura, where is this place?

00:16:13.970 --> 00:16:15.490
Mr. Harada!

00:16:17.610 --> 00:16:19.470
That guy's not Harada!

00:16:26.980 --> 00:16:28.850
Help me...

00:16:29.180 --> 00:16:30.380
Damn!

00:16:30.690 --> 00:16:32.310
Hey! Harada!

00:16:32.450 --> 00:16:35.620
Yeah, yeah! I'm doing it!

00:16:35.620 --> 00:16:39.260
Oh, I'm so against violence.
These are horrible people!

00:16:39.260 --> 00:16:40.960
What the hell are you talking about?

00:16:40.960 --> 00:16:43.660
You're the one who caused this incident!

00:16:44.770 --> 00:16:48.870
Here! Here it is! This is what's making
the system go haywire.

00:16:48.870 --> 00:16:50.060
What the?!

00:16:54.510 --> 00:16:58.150
You turned a deadly virus into an enemy

00:16:58.150 --> 00:17:01.310
and made the defenseless Mikura
battle it as a guinea pig?

00:17:01.750 --> 00:17:05.990
Since she's a volunteer, such
things are to be expected.

00:17:05.990 --> 00:17:10.590
And well, since this was an
unexpected accident...

00:17:10.590 --> 00:17:12.330
What a dangerous...

00:17:12.330 --> 00:17:14.450
Hey, bring Asami back!

00:17:14.730 --> 00:17:17.230
We can't. Since their consciousness
are connected,

00:17:17.230 --> 00:17:21.670
if we do that, there's a possibility the other girl in
the capsule might have her brain obliterated.

00:17:22.740 --> 00:17:25.810
That means until Asami drags Mikura back,

00:17:25.810 --> 00:17:28.240
all we can do is watch.

00:17:32.650 --> 00:17:34.310
Like Mikura?

00:17:34.850 --> 00:17:37.550
Right, I want to be strong.

00:17:37.790 --> 00:17:42.780
Well, going through a simulation might
be a good thing then.

00:17:43.360 --> 00:17:46.060
I know. How about carrying a good luck charm?

00:17:46.060 --> 00:17:48.730
Just by having it, you happen to
gain some confidence.

00:17:48.730 --> 00:17:49.900
How about that? What do you think?

00:17:49.900 --> 00:17:51.800
A good luck charm?

00:17:56.700 --> 00:17:58.570
What's with that?

00:17:58.570 --> 00:18:00.160
A good luck charm.

00:18:04.110 --> 00:18:07.620
Why did Mr. Harada all of a sudden disappear?

00:18:07.620 --> 00:18:09.520
How the hell would I know?

00:18:11.050 --> 00:18:11.790
What's the matter?

00:18:11.790 --> 00:18:14.690
I have my school backpack and
I'm in my normal clothes.

00:18:14.690 --> 00:18:16.590
What? You're right.

00:18:17.190 --> 00:18:20.690
Maybe we've managed to get
back to the real world?

00:18:20.690 --> 00:18:23.820
No, if that were the case, then this
annoying thing wouldn't be...

00:18:26.670 --> 00:18:29.360
It's no use, no use. You don't have to, Asami.

00:18:31.210 --> 00:18:33.910
It won't come off. I'm sorry.

00:18:33.910 --> 00:18:34.810
For what?

00:18:34.810 --> 00:18:37.850
You're going through something like this,

00:18:37.850 --> 00:18:41.840
but I can't do anything. I'm so scared.

00:18:42.820 --> 00:18:45.150
But you came to rescue me.

00:18:45.150 --> 00:18:46.950
But I...

00:18:46.950 --> 00:18:49.390
Hey, you injured your shoulder.

00:18:49.390 --> 00:18:52.380
Oh, this is just a scratch.
No problem, no problem.

00:18:52.590 --> 00:18:55.460
It's not all right, Ms. Mikura.
Please crouch down.

00:18:58.930 --> 00:19:02.230
Come to think of it, what are we running from?

00:19:04.870 --> 00:19:06.360
Hey, it's the exit!

00:19:17.220 --> 00:19:19.050
It's awfully bleak looking.

00:19:19.050 --> 00:19:21.040
How can we get home?

00:19:21.860 --> 00:19:23.410
I can hear something.

00:19:35.070 --> 00:19:37.200
Snip, snip, snip, man!

00:19:37.400 --> 00:19:39.840
The snip-snip macho! Why?!

00:19:46.580 --> 00:19:49.450
Hey, this is close to the agency.

00:19:50.780 --> 00:19:54.260
Don't resist and be fodder for my scissors.

00:19:54.260 --> 00:19:57.950
No way! Why do I have to be killed by you?!

00:19:59.430 --> 00:20:01.950
Well, I think you'd look good with
medium bobbed hair.

00:20:02.960 --> 00:20:04.530
You want to give me a haircut?!

00:20:04.530 --> 00:20:06.400
I'm a barber after all.

00:20:06.700 --> 00:20:09.640
Sorry, I prefer to go to a beauty salon.

00:20:19.910 --> 00:20:22.750
I'll just kill a girl who just won't listen!

00:20:32.160 --> 00:20:34.190
Ms. Mikura's...

00:20:34.190 --> 00:20:39.390
Hey, I was supposed to save Ms. Mikura but
what am I doing here instead?

00:21:13.300 --> 00:21:15.290
What's the point if you don't
get up on your own?

00:21:38.090 --> 00:21:42.620
Die!

00:21:49.270 --> 00:21:51.570
Mr. Kurokawa, what are you doing?

00:21:51.810 --> 00:21:55.670
Well, I happened to give her the gun
while it was still loaded.

00:21:56.510 --> 00:21:59.710
Well, thanks to that, they were both
able to come back safely

00:21:59.710 --> 00:22:01.580
so please don't ask me anything more than that.

00:22:01.580 --> 00:22:04.920
From the gun's rapid fire, the developed
systems were all destroyed.

00:22:04.920 --> 00:22:09.060
That lab manager Makura will probably have a
hard time after losing his livelihood.

00:22:09.060 --> 00:22:12.190
It serves him right for trying to make a profit
by running experiments with live subjects.

00:22:12.190 --> 00:22:13.890
What was he thinking?

00:22:13.890 --> 00:22:15.460
Did his brain swell up and he wasn't thinking
clearly after being stung by a bee or something?

00:22:15.460 --> 00:22:16.960
His future's bleak. Serves that idiot right.
It's a great victory for Mikura.

00:22:16.960 --> 00:22:18.060
And so it is. Ta-daa!

00:22:21.370 --> 00:22:24.960
Hey, I'm injured. You wrapped this up for me?

00:22:27.140 --> 00:22:29.670
Hey, it's my handkerchief.

00:22:29.840 --> 00:22:31.810
I don't remember it at all.

00:22:33.180 --> 00:22:36.180
It's a new virtual experience, allowing
you to see a dream you like!

00:22:36.180 --> 00:22:40.290
Well, it's meaningless if I don't
remember a thing.

00:22:40.290 --> 00:22:46.850
That's true. But when we came out of it,
there seemed to be quite a panic.

00:22:47.660 --> 00:22:52.120
Oh, really? I was dazed and didn't notice.

00:22:52.400 --> 00:22:55.240
Toot! Our ship is about to leave!

00:22:55.240 --> 00:22:56.930
What am I, a steam whistle?

00:23:01.580 --> 00:23:03.910
I'd like to take a peek into Pops' dream.

00:23:03.910 --> 00:23:06.650
I think you'll regret it if you do.

00:23:06.650 --> 00:23:08.180
What's that supposed to mean?

00:23:07.880 --> 00:23:09.220
Toot!

